276
00:17:08,902 --> 00:17:12,902
Uh-huh. Of course I know. He was the king!

277
00:17:13,902 --> 00:17:16,902
My men, at the height of our strength, challenged Roger to a fight.

278
00:17:17,902 --> 00:17:18,902
Really?

279
00:17:18,902 --> 00:17:19,902
A fight that we lost.

280
00:17:20,902 --> 00:17:22,902
Put in our place, we all split up.

281
00:17:25,902 --> 00:17:28,902
Everything went downhill after that. One thing led to another.

282
00:17:29,902 --> 00:17:30,902
And here I am.

283
00:17:31,902 --> 00:17:34,902
Frankly, it makes me wonder if I was worth anything to begin with.

284
00:17:35,902 --> 00:17:39,902
You fought the King of the Pirates. That means you're cool. Win or lose.

285
00:17:40,902 --> 00:17:43,902
Well, I'm not so sure. We got beaten pretty badly.

286
00:17:44,902 --> 00:17:48,902
And at any rate, we certainly didn't feel very cool. So...

287
00:17:49,902 --> 00:17:53,902
Oh, really? So Gold Roger was as tough as they say? Or tougher even?

288
00:17:54,902 --> 00:17:57,902
Yes. But one man alone can only be so strong.

289
00:17:58,902 --> 00:18:00,902
It was his crew that made him truly unstoppable.

290
00:18:01,902 --> 00:18:05,902
Or rather, it was their teamwork, their camaraderie that impressed me.

291
00:18:05,902 --> 00:18:09,902
It was an honor to see them in action.

292
00:18:10,902 --> 00:18:11,902
Oh!

293
00:18:16,902 --> 00:18:19,902
Oh, man. I guess I still got a long way to go before I'm tough like that.

294
00:18:20,902 --> 00:18:22,902
Is that so? Are you planning on being a pirate someday?

295
00:18:23,902 --> 00:18:24,902
I sure am!

296
00:18:25,902 --> 00:18:26,902
And a captain, like me.

297
00:18:27,902 --> 00:18:28,902
Mm-hmm. And a king!

298
00:18:29,902 --> 00:18:31,902
Oh, wait! You can help me! Do you have any good pirating tips?

299
00:18:31,902 --> 00:18:32,902
Mm-hmm.

300
00:18:33,902 --> 00:18:34,902
How do I get super strong?

301
00:18:35,902 --> 00:18:37,902
I gotta beat Ace and Sabo so I can be captain.

302
00:18:38,902 --> 00:18:39,902
Is that how it works?

303
00:18:40,902 --> 00:18:42,902
Uh-huh. Sure is. So can you train me?

304
00:18:42,902 --> 00:18:43,902
Well, all right.

305
00:18:44,902 --> 00:18:45,902
Really?

306
00:18:46,902 --> 00:18:49,902
That's great! I'll start my training tomorrow.

307
00:18:52,902 --> 00:18:53,902
Where did Ace go?

308
00:18:53,902 --> 00:18:55,902
Uh, yeah. About that.

309
00:18:58,902 --> 00:18:59,902
What?!

310
00:19:00,902 --> 00:19:02,902
Called Roger as Ace's dad and he never told me?!

311
00:19:02,902 --> 00:19:05,902
Yeah, well, it's a big secret. So keep it that way.

312
00:19:06,902 --> 00:19:08,902
And while you're at it, don't mention it to Ace either.

313
00:19:09,902 --> 00:19:10,902
He'll kill the both of us.

314
00:19:10,902 --> 00:19:11,902
I don't get it!

315
00:19:12,902 --> 00:19:15,902
It's a mystery to me, too. But I do know he hates Roger.

316
00:19:16,902 --> 00:19:18,902
Why? I mean, that's his dad.

317
00:19:18,902 --> 00:19:20,902
Doesn't mean he has to like him. Does it?

318
00:19:20,902 --> 00:19:27,902
I know you guys still have it worse, but even if I did have parents, I was still all alone.

319
00:19:28,902 --> 00:19:30,902
Sorry. I guess you're right.

320
00:19:31,902 --> 00:19:35,902
Family or not, I guess some people in this world just aren't meant to get along.

321
00:19:36,902 --> 00:19:39,902
Yeah, but most people don't have the King of the Pirates as their dad.

322
00:19:40,902 --> 00:19:43,902
I know you want to ask him about Roger, and to be honest, I'd love to know myself.

323
00:19:44,902 --> 00:19:45,902
But just lay off, okay? Do you promise?

324
00:19:45,902 --> 00:19:47,902
Uh-huh, no problem.

325
00:19:48,902 --> 00:19:50,902
Oh, and you too, Nagari.

326
00:19:51,902 --> 00:19:52,902
I won't say a word.

327
00:19:54,902 --> 00:19:59,902
But to think that Roger had a son, and he was right here all this time.

328
00:20:00,902 --> 00:20:01,902
All right, there he is.

329
00:20:02,902 --> 00:20:05,902
Looks like he calmed down, but play it cool just in case, got it?

330
00:20:06,902 --> 00:20:07,902
Yeah. And do not mention Roger.

331
00:20:07,902 --> 00:20:08,902
I know, I know, I know.

332
00:20:08,902 --> 00:20:13,902
Hey, Ace, there you are. Didn't know you came home already.

333
00:20:14,902 --> 00:20:18,902
Hey, Ace, there you are. Didn't know Roger was your dad and you hate him.

334
00:20:19,902 --> 00:20:21,902
He didn't last five seconds.

335
00:20:22,902 --> 00:20:26,902
Remember when we were going to drown you, because I'm kind of regretting that we did it right now.

336
00:20:26,902 --> 00:20:27,902
Luffy.

337
00:20:28,902 --> 00:20:29,902
Yeah?

338
00:20:30,902 --> 00:20:31,902
Who told you all that?

339
00:20:33,902 --> 00:20:34,902
Sabo did!

340
00:20:35,902 --> 00:20:38,902
So tell me, was Roger awesome or super awesome?

341
00:20:39,902 --> 00:20:44,902
Stop it! Be cool! This is the exact opposite of what I told you to do! You're gonna get us killed!

342
00:20:45,902 --> 00:20:47,902
Ow!

343
00:20:48,902 --> 00:20:51,902
Don't you ever speak that name in front of me again, got it?

344
00:20:52,902 --> 00:20:57,902
Don't be stingy, I bet you got cool stories to tell.

345
00:20:58,902 --> 00:21:00,902
You could have let me explain before you clobbered me over the head.

346
00:21:01,902 --> 00:21:02,902
That's enough!

347
00:21:03,902 --> 00:21:04,902
There!

348
00:21:05,902 --> 00:21:07,902
I wanna hear pirate secrets, please!

349
00:21:08,902 --> 00:21:10,902
Yeah! We're brothers, we can't hide things from each other!

350
00:21:11,902 --> 00:21:13,902
Shut up! You're both dead to me!

351
00:21:14,902 --> 00:21:16,902
Roger, Roger, Roger! He's your father, father, father!

352
00:21:17,902 --> 00:21:19,902
Stop! His anger's making him stronger!

353
00:21:19,902 --> 00:21:23,902
This is your fault for running your mouth in the first place, Sabo!

354
00:21:24,902 --> 00:21:25,902
Ow! He had to learn someday!

355
00:21:26,902 --> 00:21:27,902
No kidding me!

356
00:21:33,902 --> 00:21:37,902
Let me say it again. From now on, you bastards are dead to me.

357
00:21:38,902 --> 00:21:40,902
Oh yeah? Took the words out of my mouth!

358
00:21:41,902 --> 00:21:42,902
Ugh!

359
00:21:46,902 --> 00:21:48,902
Don't let me down, I'll be counting on you.

360
00:21:49,902 --> 00:21:52,902
Got it. I'll leave no stone unturned.

361
00:21:55,902 --> 00:21:56,902
Well, you heard the man.

362
00:21:57,902 --> 00:21:58,902
We'll get right on it, boss.

363
00:21:59,902 --> 00:22:02,902
Hold on. When you find him, don't do anything yet.

364
00:22:02,902 --> 00:22:03,902
What?

365
00:22:03,902 --> 00:22:07,902
The longer we make him wait, the more gratitude we can wring out of him.

366
00:22:08,902 --> 00:22:10,902
Money's fine, but I want a favor, too.

367
00:22:11,902 --> 00:22:13,902
He can wait for his dear Sabo a bit longer.

368
00:22:14,902 --> 00:22:15,902
I see.

369
00:22:16,902 --> 00:22:19,902
Keep an eye on him, but until I give you the order, don't snatch him up.

370
00:22:19,902 --> 00:22:22,902
We will have a visit this spring.

371
00:22:23,902 --> 00:22:24,902
Dogra! Mangra!

372
00:22:25,902 --> 00:22:27,902
What is Goa? A country?

373
00:22:28,902 --> 00:22:30,902
Uh, that's the country we live in.

374
00:22:31,902 --> 00:22:34,902
Mount Corvo, Windmill Village, and Great Terminal are all part of Goa.

375
00:22:35,902 --> 00:22:36,902
Hmph. I knew that.

376
00:22:37,902 --> 00:22:38,902
It must be the end of the world.

377
00:22:39,902 --> 00:22:41,902
I wasn't even sure you could read, and now you're reading the paper.

378
00:22:42,902 --> 00:22:43,902
Frankly, it's kinda creeping me out.

379
00:22:43,902 --> 00:22:52,902
Anyway, they're making a big deal about this visit, but it's not like they're gonna haul their asses all the way to our mountain.

380
00:22:53,902 --> 00:22:56,902
Not that I'd want to see those pompous bastards anyway.

381
00:22:57,902 --> 00:22:59,902
Celestial Dragons, no thanks.

382
00:22:59,902 --> 00:23:13,902
Ace and Sabo visit Nagari to see how Luffy is faring in his new apprenticeship.

383
00:23:14,902 --> 00:23:20,902
As the three boys compete to decide who will be captain, Nagari reminds them that it takes more than strength to be a leader.

384
00:23:21,902 --> 00:23:25,902
Facing off with a massive tiger, they must find their answer in battle.

385
00:23:25,902 --> 00:23:29,902
On the next, One Piece! The battle against the big tiger!

386
00:23:30,902 --> 00:23:33,902
Who is going to be captain? I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

